# Required positive matrix once implemented:
#   1. self source -> self MIR -> admitted general C, direct/admitted C equal
#   2. self runtime == native C runtime == native LLVM runtime
#   3. success: A/B payloads consumed, UndoA=0, UndoB=0
#   4. B failure: exact failure payload consumed, UndoA=1, UndoB=0, state restored
#
# Required valid-identity MIR mutations, each rejected before any C artifact:
#   outcome-binding-definition-or-type-cross-wire
#     diagnostic: MIR intent step outcome binding is invalid
#   outcome-variant-or-successor-cross-wire
#     diagnostic: MIR intent step outcome branch identity is invalid
#   predecessor-self-future-or-mixed-identity
#     diagnostic: MIR intent compensation predecessor evidence is invalid
#   missing-success-completion-with-compensation-present
#     diagnostic: MIR intent step completion evidence is missing
#
# This gate may be renamed to .sh and registered only in the same change that
# supplies the real owner, fixture, observed positive/parity results, and all
# fail-closed mutations. A documentation-only PASS is forbidden.
